The analytic AgX base-look and fitted ACES preview transforms are adapted from three.js:
https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/dev/src/renderers/shaders/ShaderChunk/tonemapping_pars_fragment.glsl.js
Its implementation follows Filament's Blender-derived Rec.2020 AgX transform
and the minimal AgX default-contrast polynomial approximation.
Adaptations: shared preview exposure/sRGB encoding, explicit zero-input guard,
no optional look, and no three.js dependency. This is an analytic approximation,
not Blender's complete OpenColorIO configuration.
The ACES transform uses Stephen Hill's fitted RRT/ODT and input/output matrices,
including three.js's 1/0.6 viewing-environment scale. Its rational fit is evaluated
in a scaled form to avoid HDR overflow. It is not the full ACES reference pipeline.
Original fitted transform: https://github.com/selfshadow/ltc_code/blob/master/webgl/shaders/ltc/ltc_blit.fs

